## 1. Scope

This reference covers cold shrink terminations and joints for 12/20 kV cable, a voltage class widely used in European distribution. The content is written around the fit between accessory and cable geometry, which is the recurring reason an approved accessory underperforms on site.

## 2. Construction

- Pre-expanded insulating sleeve with moulded geometric stress cone and conductive screen deflector.
- Silicone or EPDM body selected for the required creepage and the expected pollution level.
- Sealing parts at the sheath and the terminal end, supplied as part of the kit rather than as loose consumables.
- Outdoor variants with shed profile; indoor variants with a plain insulating body.

